# Copy to `.env.local` for the values that are yours rather than the project's: every secret, and
# anything that differs between machines. `.env.local` is gitignored; this example is not.
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# Nothing here is required. Every variable has a working default in the committed `.env`, so
# diele runs without this file at all — it exists for what cannot be committed, and as the place
# to override a default without editing a tracked file.
#
# Precedence, most specific first, first match wins:
#
#   1. a real environment variable          what a container is given; images ship no .env
#   2. api/.env.local   web/.env.local      package, untracked
#   3. api/.env         web/.env            package, committed — ships fully commented out
#   4. .env.local                           repo, untracked          <- this file
#   5. .env                                 repo, committed          <- every variable, defaulted
#   6. the built-in default                 api/src/config.ts
#
# The nearest scope wins outright and, within a scope, the untracked file beats the committed
# one. That is the usual monorepo convention composed with the usual dotenv one. It works because
# `api/.env` and `web/.env` ship with every line commented out: they are override slots, not a
# second place where defaults live. Put a live value in one and it outranks this file.
#
# Every variable below is listed with its committed default, so overriding one is uncommenting
# rather than going to look it up.

# ── secrets, which have no default ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Keys connector credentials are encrypted with, as a comma separated list of `id:base64` pairs.
# The first is the active one, so rotating means prepending a new key and leaving the old ones
# behind to open what they already sealed. Generate one with:
#
#   echo "k1:$(openssl rand -base64 32)"
#
# Unset is not fatal: diele boots, connectors stop syncing and say why. Losing the key means
# re-entering every credential by hand, so back it up somewhere other than the database.
DIELE_SECRET_KEYS=

# Local mode only. Creating the first account is the one action there is nobody to authenticate
# for, so the setup form asks for this. Left unset, the server generates one and prints it at
# startup, which is the safe default; set it to script an install.
#LOCAL_SETUP_TOKEN=

# ── sign-in ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# One of `local`, `oidc` or `dev`, and only ever one line: dotenv keeps the last value it sees for
# a repeated key, so a second uncommented AUTH_MODE further down silently outranks the first.
#
# `local` keeps accounts in the database and signs them in with a password. The first account is
# created through a setup form gated by the token above, so an unclaimed instance is not open.
#
# `oidc` runs the real authorization code flow against any compliant issuer, and needs the block
# below filled in.
#
# `dev` grants every login as a fixed local identity, so the web app can be worked on without
# signing in. Never set this on anything reachable by others.
#AUTH_MODE=local

# Only read when AUTH_MODE=oidc. The issuer is the application's base url, the one whose
# .well-known/openid-configuration answers; register http://localhost:5173/api/auth/callback as a
# redirect uri alongside the production one.
#OIDC_ISSUER=https://sso.example.com/application/o/diele/
#OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
#OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
#OIDC_SCOPES="openid email profile"
#OIDC_DISPLAY_NAME="Single Sign-On"

# ── the two halves ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Moving the api off :3000 means telling the dev server where it went, so these two travel
# together.
#PORT=3000
#VITE_API_TARGET=http://localhost:3000

# Origin the browser reaches diele on. The OIDC redirect uri is derived from it.
#PUBLIC_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# ── storage ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Created and migrated on boot; delete the file to start over. A relative path is resolved from
# the repo root, so it lands in ./data/ whichever directory npm ran from.
#DB_PATH="data/diele.db"

# ── sessions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Idle windows rather than lifetimes: both roll forward on every use, so an instance opened daily
# never asks again. The second is what `remember me` picks at login.
#SESSION_MAX_AGE_MS=86400000
#SESSION_REMEMBER_MAX_AGE_MS=7776000000

# Defaults to on when PUBLIC_ORIGIN is https and off otherwise, which is almost always right. A
# secure cookie sent to an http origin is dropped by the browser without a word, and the login
# then answers 200 while staying signed out.
#SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE=false

# ── appearance ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The wordmark and the line under it. The subtitle is uppercased and letter-spaced by the web
# app, so write it in ordinary case.
#BRAND_TITLE="diele"
#BRAND_SUBTITLE="start page"

# The accent: the tilde in the wordmark, and every hover and focus state. One value per theme,
# six-digit hex only.
#BRAND_ACCENT_LIGHT="#16a34a"
#BRAND_ACCENT_DARK="#22c55e"
